No, the game is not 'too easy after a certain point'. It is just different
after a certain point. On early levels you fight mainly against the random
number generator, an experienced player will have higher probability of 
surviving than a newbie, but still has a good chance of being killed. 
But later during play the game balance shifts somewhat - it's not the
sheer number and power of monsters that kill you, it is rather your lack 
of knowledge how to deal with a new, unexpected situation... Puzzles appear 
that you have to solve in order to proceed. Once you solved the game (or 
read all the spoilers) you'll have no problems at this stage - but show me 
an unspoiled player who never got killed by the Medusa...

To say it in a different way: The later stages of the game are not easy;
they just have low replayability. Some people try co compare nethack vs.
moria - moria is just the same all over, only monsters grow more powerful
as you do. Nethack actually changes as you get deeper and deeper...

